WEBVTT

00:13.847 --> 00:18.309
Those who ceaselessly hone
their killing arts are known as "Masters."

00:18.727 --> 00:23.814
After many generations,
they have gained lethal abilities

00:23.815 --> 00:26.276
called "Modified Bloodlines."

00:27.068 --> 00:32.698
This is the story of one such Master,
the Poison Master, Hikaru Gero,

00:32.699 --> 00:35.243
and his attempts to get married.

00:43.752 --> 00:47.296
Locked in Latata

00:47.297 --> 00:50.966
Secrets in my veins Latata

00:50.967 --> 00:52.760
I know you want it

00:52.761 --> 00:54.553
And sure, I love it

00:54.554 --> 00:58.807
So I stay behind the mask Latata

00:58.808 --> 01:02.144
Run, run, run back to back Run

01:02.145 --> 01:06.023
Fun, fun, fun unpredictable but fun

01:06.024 --> 01:08.233
At the end of every mind game

01:08.234 --> 01:12.196
Shoot through the darkened night

01:12.197 --> 01:15.407
Poisoned in our bodies still

01:15.408 --> 01:20.079
Laugh at us our reckless souls

01:20.080 --> 01:21.413
TOXIC

01:21.414 --> 01:23.707
For you I will

01:23.708 --> 01:25.000
TOXIC

01:25.001 --> 01:27.419
Rewrite my destiny

01:27.420 --> 01:30.923
Losing it, falling for you

01:30.924 --> 01:34.384
What's tomorrow Kill or Kiss

01:34.385 --> 01:35.594
TOXIC

01:35.595 --> 01:37.930
Tell me what you want

01:37.931 --> 01:39.181
TOXIC

01:39.182 --> 01:41.475
I'll stay right here

01:41.476 --> 01:44.937
Like a spell, I'll be by your side

01:44.938 --> 01:48.608
What you gonna do Kill or Kiss

01:52.529 --> 01:55.115
Kill or Kiss

01:56.199 --> 01:58.660
Kill or Kiss

01:59.744 --> 02:01.996
Kill or Kiss

02:07.585 --> 02:09.879
The Bug Master, Toshiki Hanamaki.

02:10.255 --> 02:14.341
He's a longtime colleague,
as well as my friend.

02:14.342 --> 02:17.845
W-Wow. So it's this guy's wedding, huh?

02:17.846 --> 02:19.972
He's just what I picture
when I hear "Master."

02:19.973 --> 02:21.765
W-Well, have fun.

02:21.766 --> 02:22.934
Hey, Kinosaki.

02:25.270 --> 02:27.939
There's a butterfly for you, too.

02:29.149 --> 02:31.316
"Dear Mei Kinosaki,"

02:31.317 --> 02:35.238
"How do you do? I hope you aren't
sweltering in this early summer heat."

02:35.947 --> 02:38.074
"Mr. Gero has informed me
of your arrangement."

02:38.449 --> 02:42.912
"I cannot thank you enough for taking
the time to help him find a partner."

02:43.204 --> 02:48.960
"Nothing would please me more than you
accompanying him to my humble wedding."

02:49.460 --> 02:52.589
"Please allow me to express
my gratitude in person."

02:52.922 --> 02:55.633
"Yours truly,
Toshiki Hanamaki, Bug Master."

02:57.719 --> 02:58.887
How's he such a great guy?

02:59.387 --> 03:02.806
This is a first for me,
so I don't have the right clothes.

03:02.807 --> 03:06.935
Still, I want to get things right
for his wedding, you know?

03:06.936 --> 03:08.687
That's the spirit.

03:08.688 --> 03:11.649
And there's always a chance
you'll meet someone new at a wedding.

03:11.941 --> 03:14.651
I think I'll pick up a new outfit, too.

03:14.652 --> 03:16.195
Your treat, okay?

03:31.878 --> 03:34.963
And here we are
at the Bug Master's wedding.

03:34.964 --> 03:37.717
It's ten times more "fairy tale"
than I was expecting.

03:47.060 --> 03:48.186
Gero!

03:52.440 --> 03:53.524
Gero, you-

03:54.442 --> 03:55.860
You came back to life?!

03:56.402 --> 03:59.155
You're wicked worn out, boss man.

03:59.489 --> 04:01.824
Been leanin' too hard
on your Modified Bloodline.

04:02.200 --> 04:04.410
That was a pick-me-up,
but it's only so effective.

04:04.953 --> 04:05.953
Uh...

04:05.954 --> 04:08.830
Kinosaki, let me introduce you.
This guy...

04:08.831 --> 04:13.001
is Tsunagi, the Needle Master.
Like the Bug Master, he's a friend of mine.

04:13.002 --> 04:14.337
Always happy to help.

04:15.046 --> 04:17.756
Hey, boys. We've got money to burn.

04:17.757 --> 04:20.260
Who's up for Undeadsney Land this weekend?

04:21.386 --> 04:23.595
Will we get to meet Undeadsney, Pa?

04:23.596 --> 04:24.638
You bet.

04:24.639 --> 04:26.682
And the optimal route
for the attractions?

04:26.683 --> 04:27.724
You can plan it.

04:27.725 --> 04:29.434
He's a good dad.

04:29.435 --> 04:31.062
He has three boys.

04:31.354 --> 04:35.108
Oh, so you're the boss man's
marriage advisor, huh?

04:35.733 --> 04:37.818
Must be rough. I feel for you.

04:37.819 --> 04:39.737
You can tell?

04:41.114 --> 04:42.699
Honored guests,

04:43.032 --> 04:47.912
we cannot thank you enough
for taking the time to join us today.

04:50.415 --> 04:55.670
We will now celebrate the union between
Toshiki Hanamaki and Anna Kawakita.

05:03.469 --> 05:08.016
If the sun... is ever going to rise
on the criminal underworld,

05:08.266 --> 05:12.477
the organ trafficking networks...
and the drug cartels...

05:12.478 --> 05:14.814
must link hands in unity.

05:15.106 --> 05:21.112
I aspire to end... the criminal underworld's
long period of forced isolation...

05:29.037 --> 05:30.912
I'm glad to see you.

05:30.913 --> 05:33.791
I only came to warn you in person.

05:34.208 --> 05:36.960
Listen up. You can try to curry favor
with me all you like,

05:36.961 --> 05:39.881
but it won't get Grandma
to treat your clan any better than-

05:42.592 --> 05:45.635
Oh, sorry if I gave you
the wrong impression.

05:45.636 --> 05:48.556
I just wanted to have a drink together.

05:49.140 --> 05:51.601
With you, Hikaru Gero.

05:56.856 --> 05:58.483
Won't you join me?

05:59.442 --> 06:02.487
You're underage, so it's not alcoholic.

06:04.697 --> 06:06.741
Gero, did you hear that?

06:06.991 --> 06:08.825
Huh? What?

06:08.826 --> 06:10.745
How they met.

06:11.037 --> 06:15.124
The bride, Anna, got into trouble
while mountain-climbing, and...

06:15.708 --> 06:17.210
That's so like him.

06:54.497 --> 06:55.623
Kinosaki.

06:56.666 --> 07:00.961
Do you think I can pull off
a marriage this perfect?

07:00.962 --> 07:04.090
Of course. You've got me in your corner.

07:07.301 --> 07:09.011
Congratulations, Toshiki.

07:21.441 --> 07:26.529
You've got plenty of happiness
and plenty of love. Don't you, Bug Master?

07:26.904 --> 07:29.323
How is that fair?

07:34.454 --> 07:38.124
They met in the mountains
and now spend their days camping.

07:42.670 --> 07:44.338
I'll take another chateaubriand!

07:46.966 --> 07:48.301
Wait, Gero!

07:48.509 --> 07:50.635
You're supposed to give
a speech after this!

07:50.636 --> 07:52.430
Kinosaki, take over for me.

07:52.722 --> 07:55.183
Huh? What's with the spider?

07:56.350 --> 07:57.935
You said it, Julia Jr.

07:58.352 --> 08:02.690
You're his partners. You want to keep
his wedding unmarred even more than I do.

08:05.026 --> 08:09.030
I mean, this is the best day
of Toshiki's life. Right?

08:10.865 --> 08:16.245
In exactly five minutes,
all of you rush your assigned entrances,

08:16.537 --> 08:20.499
and kill whoever you want.
The more corpses, the bigger your bonus.

08:20.500 --> 08:26.963
You can leave when the Bug Master
and his Master friends start fighting back.

08:26.964 --> 08:31.301
While they're distracted,
I'll stick a "firework" on the bride.

08:31.302 --> 08:34.054
I bet she'll make a real pretty color
when she goes off.

08:34.055 --> 08:38.809
One he'll never be able to forget,
even if he wants to.

08:44.106 --> 08:47.859
Guess that's what I get
for hiring mercs on the Dark Nav.

08:47.860 --> 08:50.029
Well, in that case...

08:50.530 --> 08:52.782
Change of plans.

09:02.375 --> 09:05.002
Firestorm Labyrinth!

09:05.670 --> 09:08.088
Aw, what a waste.

09:08.089 --> 09:12.969
I set those to give the fleeing guests
a real-life escape game.

09:13.386 --> 09:16.888
Aw, man. Well, it's his own fault
for getting in my way.

09:16.889 --> 09:21.101
All that matters right now
is paying back the Bug Master,

09:21.102 --> 09:25.690
the man who stole the only spark
of passion in my life.

09:26.107 --> 09:31.820
Yeah. Back then, nothing mattered to me.

09:31.821 --> 09:36.700
School, jobs, marriage.
It all made me go, "So what?"

09:36.701 --> 09:39.578
Even when I ended up buried in debt,

09:39.579 --> 09:41.455
I just went, "Yeah, so?"

09:44.166 --> 09:48.086
And when my "payment" meant someone
calling himself the Puppet Master

09:48.087 --> 09:51.548
"customizing" me into
a hitman for some gang,

09:51.549 --> 09:54.385
I just went, "Oh, yeah?"

09:57.221 --> 09:58.680
Yamada.

09:58.681 --> 10:06.564
I've planted miniature bombs
in your wrists, ankles, and head.

10:07.440 --> 10:11.359
Press the switch in your back tooth
at the moment of impact,

10:11.360 --> 10:14.530
and your enemy will explode along
with your own flesh and bone.

10:15.281 --> 10:17.325
An Explosion Roulette.

10:18.242 --> 10:22.496
Trash exists only to die with grace.

10:28.878 --> 10:32.256
If worse came to worst, I could just
take my opponent down with me.

10:32.923 --> 10:40.348
The Explosion Roulette sparked
my passion for the first time ever.

10:44.352 --> 10:46.896
Until I met him.

11:05.331 --> 11:06.956
I've got him!

11:06.957 --> 11:11.336
If I set off my ace in the hole,
the bomb in my head,

11:11.337 --> 11:13.089
I can trade my life for...

11:16.425 --> 11:17.676
I disarmed it.

11:18.135 --> 11:20.846
You don't need to live
in fear of death anymore.

11:25.434 --> 11:31.398
And that's how he took my passion from me,
just so he could feel good about himself!

11:31.399 --> 11:36.319
So don't I have the right to break
something that means a lot to him?

11:36.320 --> 11:39.823
I got new limbs as an advance
from the Puppet Master,

11:39.824 --> 11:45.578
made out like a bandit doing dirty jobs,
and waited for this day to come.

11:45.579 --> 11:47.581
Anyone who gets in my way is-

11:47.998 --> 11:50.793
Oh, hey. He's already dead.

11:51.794 --> 11:54.379
Yeah, go with that, Kinosaki.

11:54.380 --> 11:56.173
I need you to fill in for me.

11:57.216 --> 12:00.010
Sushi? Sure thing.

12:01.720 --> 12:03.514
Did you say something?

12:04.682 --> 12:07.600
Oh well. I don't know what your deal is,

12:07.601 --> 12:10.521
but nobody nice holds a grudge
against the Bug Master.

12:11.105 --> 12:13.858
We don't need your lame sideshow.

12:16.068 --> 12:19.321
Now, let's hear from
a friend of the groom.

12:21.157 --> 12:25.744
I'm gonna make Gero treat me to sushi
that costs hundreds of thousands of yen.

12:28.038 --> 12:29.999
(The Bug Master's Wedding)

12:30.958 --> 12:33.293
It's really pouring now, huh?

12:33.294 --> 12:36.088
So much for the gorgeous view
of the sunset.

12:37.131 --> 12:41.968
Now, a word from a friend of the groom,
Mr. Toshiki Hanamaki: Mr. Hikaru Gero.

12:41.969 --> 12:43.219
Or not?

12:43.220 --> 12:46.264
Stage fright gave Gero an upset stomach.

12:46.265 --> 12:49.225
He left a letter for me
to read in his place.

12:49.226 --> 12:51.312
My name is Mei Kinosaki.

12:58.569 --> 13:01.988
Hey, buddy. You're a Master, right?

13:01.989 --> 13:04.616
Don't you think you'd better
stop holding back

13:04.617 --> 13:07.411
with your Modified Bloodline?

13:10.080 --> 13:12.333
I wouldn't waste it on you.

13:13.876 --> 13:16.086
"Toshiki, Anna..."

13:16.420 --> 13:17.963
"Congratulations on your marriage."

13:18.380 --> 13:22.384
"That's not something I ever thought
I'd say. I still can't believe it."

13:23.677 --> 13:24.720
"Toshiki."

13:26.013 --> 13:29.224
"I'm looking for a bride
myself right now,

13:29.225 --> 13:32.061
and it's hard as hell."

13:34.438 --> 13:40.528
"The old me would have snapped,
'Not a chance! You're wasting your time!'"

13:41.987 --> 13:48.744
"But here I am, hoping to meet
the one for me. And that..."

13:49.161 --> 13:52.331
"That's because of you, Toshiki."

13:54.625 --> 13:55.668
"Toshiki..."

13:56.210 --> 13:59.462
"Tell me. Back when I was
like a prickly ghost,

13:59.463 --> 14:01.423
why did you decide to care about me?"

14:03.676 --> 14:06.303
"On behalf of past me,
I'd like to thank you."

14:07.513 --> 14:08.931
"If it wasn't for you..."

14:10.140 --> 14:12.768
"I'm sure I'd still be..."

14:21.110 --> 14:23.153
Nice aim, you-

14:25.573 --> 14:31.161
"You don't let anything stop you from
reaching out to someone who's suffering."

14:32.663 --> 14:37.293
"That's what makes you my best friend,
and the coolest guy I know."

14:40.170 --> 14:42.965
I don't want to make this special day
a bloody one.

14:43.465 --> 14:44.550
So leave.

14:46.218 --> 14:49.178
Seems you're having trouble, Yamada.

14:49.179 --> 14:51.223
I stand by my products.

14:51.515 --> 14:53.850
I'll release your limiters.

14:53.851 --> 14:58.230
You'll blow them all away with
a blast wave that hits like a typhoon.

15:04.486 --> 15:08.490
Just you wait, Bug Master!

15:21.253 --> 15:22.962
Damn it.

15:22.963 --> 15:25.007
How's that fair?

15:25.716 --> 15:33.057
You hang out in a way deeper,
darker underworld than a hitman like me.

15:34.099 --> 15:38.562
So how can you hug an enemy so gently?

15:39.939 --> 15:42.232
Yamada, you're going the wrong-

15:43.192 --> 15:44.776
Don't tell me you're...

15:44.777 --> 15:48.030
Shit. Shit! Damn it all!

15:49.073 --> 15:52.034
Have a farewell present from me!

15:52.826 --> 15:55.203
"Finally, to Anna.

15:55.204 --> 15:58.624
It goes without saying,
but the moment you found Toshiki...

16:02.336 --> 16:04.755
your happy ending was guaranteed."

16:06.590 --> 16:07.675
It ends there.

16:08.008 --> 16:09.510
Thank you for listening.

16:14.765 --> 16:17.601
I'd like you all to take a look
out the window.

16:25.859 --> 16:26.944
Toshiki.

16:29.363 --> 16:30.406
Congratulations.

16:45.713 --> 16:48.589
Kinosaki, thank you.

16:48.590 --> 16:51.968
For the speech, and for helping Gero.

16:51.969 --> 16:53.887
Oh, it's no big deal.

16:54.221 --> 16:57.557
Anyway, don't you think
you're a little too nice to him?

16:57.558 --> 17:01.687
You've been looking out for Gero
since he was all rough around the edges.

17:02.771 --> 17:06.734
Well, to tell you the truth,
I should be the one thanking him.

17:08.068 --> 17:10.486
With the power dynamic
between our families,

17:10.487 --> 17:14.490
him calling me his friend
and coming to my wedding

17:14.491 --> 17:17.201
is more than I have a right to hope for.

17:17.202 --> 17:23.125
What power dynamics?
Aren't you a Master, just like Gero?

17:26.837 --> 17:30.006
The Hanamaki family of Bug Masters
started with venomous insects.

17:30.007 --> 17:33.009
The Tsunagi family of Needle Masters
started with poisoned needles.

17:33.010 --> 17:38.097
There are plenty of other Masters,
like the disease guys,

17:38.098 --> 17:42.269
but our branch families
all descend from the Poison Clan.

17:42.644 --> 17:45.481
So our hierarchy is set in stone,

17:45.981 --> 17:48.776
with the Five Great Families at the top.

17:49.526 --> 17:50.527
The Gero family.

17:51.153 --> 17:52.237
The Arima family.

17:53.030 --> 17:54.073
The Dogo family.

17:54.656 --> 17:55.783
The Kirishima family.

17:56.408 --> 17:57.493
The Nasu family.

17:59.078 --> 18:04.750
The whole society of Masters is made up
of their branches and offshoots.

18:05.250 --> 18:08.045
Occasionally, you do get
an unaffiliated family,

18:08.837 --> 18:12.757
but those of the branch families and below
would end their lives without complaint,

18:12.758 --> 18:14.510
if their Great Family ordered it.

18:15.010 --> 18:17.429
That's how big the difference is.

18:19.389 --> 18:21.140
Listen, Toshiki.

18:21.141 --> 18:25.813
We live only on the sufferance
of the Gero family.

18:27.272 --> 18:29.440
Centuries of toying with lives

18:29.441 --> 18:33.362
has made monsters of the heads
of the Five Great Families.

18:33.821 --> 18:35.738
Don't assume they share our values.

18:35.739 --> 18:41.160
They see the lives of enemies and allies
as mere pawns to enrich their clans.

18:41.161 --> 18:45.791
Unless you want our line to end,
just be silent and obey.

19:00.931 --> 19:04.017
Oh, it's quite all right.
Raise your heads.

19:07.354 --> 19:11.483
This is Master Hikaru. He was tentatively
named heir the other day.

19:12.526 --> 19:17.739
When I first met Gero, rather than
fearing him, what struck me

19:18.615 --> 19:19.867
was how he seemed, well...

19:23.579 --> 19:29.126
We lowly worms owe our very lives
to the Gero family's generosity.

19:29.626 --> 19:31.252
Well, let's leave it at that.

19:31.253 --> 19:32.671
Y-Yes, sir.

19:33.922 --> 19:35.215
Master Hikaru!

19:35.674 --> 19:40.179
Please use and discard his life
as you would a lowly insect's.

19:42.389 --> 19:44.433
I beg of you.

19:55.235 --> 19:56.862
He's not a bug, though.

20:02.826 --> 20:04.076
He seemed like...

20:04.077 --> 20:07.288
it wasn't his fault
people trembled in fear of him.

20:07.289 --> 20:09.333
He was really just a guy.

20:10.709 --> 20:12.711
A regular, stand-up guy.

20:14.171 --> 20:16.215
When I told my father
we were drinking buddies,

20:16.465 --> 20:18.675
he passed out foaming at the mouth.

20:21.053 --> 20:22.095
Ms. Kinosaki.

20:29.811 --> 20:34.274
I'm sure it'll be a hundred times more
hassle than for me or the Needle Clan,

20:35.317 --> 20:37.945
but please make him ridiculously happy.

20:40.864 --> 20:43.741
Oh, it's tough, all right.

20:43.742 --> 20:46.452
He tends to freak out
in front of girls, for one thing.

20:46.453 --> 20:48.121
Well, you know how it is.

20:48.622 --> 20:52.751
But I know he's a good guy
as well as you do.

20:53.502 --> 20:59.424
I promise I'll find her.
Gero's partner for life.

21:03.971 --> 21:07.891
Kinosaki's been bonding with my colleagues
while I wasn't looking.

21:08.600 --> 21:10.894
What are they up to?

21:14.064 --> 21:16.482
Call me if you're gonna go fight.

21:16.483 --> 21:18.694
You have kids to take care of.

21:23.782 --> 21:24.825
Toshiki.

21:25.617 --> 21:28.287
Have a hundred million blessings.

21:34.960 --> 21:37.337
Be happy!

21:47.973 --> 21:49.391
Y-Yeah.

21:49.850 --> 21:52.768
He had a blade on a long pole,

21:52.769 --> 21:55.397
and he was really good
at waving it around.

21:55.689 --> 21:57.649
Uh-huh. Only...

21:58.233 --> 22:01.111
Apart from that,
he was kind of, um, normal?

22:01.528 --> 22:02.988
Great work.

22:03.864 --> 22:06.908
Okay, I'll send you
the next list of Masters now.

22:08.160 --> 22:10.412
Good luck wiping out those hitmen.

22:12.873 --> 22:13.707
(Poison Master
Hikaru Gero)

22:28.680 --> 22:30.973
Ah! Something smells fishy!

22:30.974 --> 22:32.892
I'm shocked, startled,
it's adding insult to injury

22:32.893 --> 22:34.226
I'm completely obsessed

22:34.227 --> 22:36.604
Ah! Something smells off!

22:36.605 --> 22:38.606
You're all bluff,
I'm sick and tired, so disappointed

22:38.607 --> 22:39.649
Bye-bye, mwah!

22:39.941 --> 22:42.777
It seems like I'm only good at

22:42.778 --> 22:45.613
workbooks for a child

22:45.614 --> 22:48.365
Even through infectious disease,
I want to love with you

22:48.366 --> 22:51.327
No! No! Love's in gridlock!

22:51.328 --> 22:53.829
Forever and ever, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

22:53.830 --> 22:57.041
Darling, heading toward a twisted signpost

22:57.042 --> 22:59.543
Heart fluttering, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

22:59.544 --> 23:02.297
Just the two of us, consolation prize

23:12.557 --> 23:14.767
Ah, the scent of dance

23:14.768 --> 23:16.602
I'm completely obsessed

23:16.603 --> 23:18.020
with you as you flutter down

23:18.021 --> 23:20.272
Ah, something smells off

23:20.273 --> 23:22.483
I'm blown away by you

23:22.484 --> 23:23.484
Bye-bye, mwah!

23:23.485 --> 23:26.612
It seems like I'm only good at

23:26.613 --> 23:29.365
workbooks for a child

23:29.366 --> 23:32.201
I want us to share even our growing pains

23:32.202 --> 23:34.871
No! No! Love's in gridlock!

23:35.080 --> 23:37.665
Forever and ever, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

23:37.666 --> 23:40.751
Darling, heading toward
a stagnant signpost

23:40.752 --> 23:43.337
Heart fluttering, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

23:43.338 --> 23:46.091
